### Summary of behavior

| Aspect | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| `-p` / `--parents` | Creates all missing intermediate components; idempotent on existing dirs (incl. symlink→dir) |
| Intermediate mode | `0777 & ~umask`, then `chmod` to guarantee owner `w+x` (0300) |
| Final mode | `0777 & ~umask` (no extra chmod) |
| Existing non-dir in path | Fails with `ENOTDIR` diagnostic |
| Broken symlink in path | Fails with `ENOTDIR` diagnostic (detected via `lstat`) |
| Repeated/trailing slashes, `.` | Skipped during component walk; normal pathname semantics preserved |
| Non-p mode | Unchanged: single `mkdir(operand, 0777)` |
| Options after operands | Supported (both passes scan all args) |
| `--` terminator | Everything after is a literal operand (including `-p`) |
| Exit code | 0 only if every operand succeeded; 1 otherwise |
| Memory | One `malloc(len+1)` per operand in `-p` mode; freed before return |
